 "足し前": "ملحق (An extension to a document or publication that adds information, corrects errors) / مُكَمِّل (A vitamin, herbal extract, or chemical compound ingested to meet dietary deficie)  [supplement]",
 "足し算": "إضَافَة (The act of adding anything.) / مُضَاف (Anything that is added.) / جَمْع (The arithmetic operation of adding.)  [addition]\nمثال: うちの息子はまだちゃんと足し算ができない。\n→ My boy can't do addition properly yet.",
 "足す": "جَمَعَ (To sum up; to put together mentally; to add up.) / أَضَافَ (To append (e.g. a statement); to say further information.) / أَضَافَ (To intensify; to augment; to increase.) / أَضَافَ (To add someone as a friend.)  [to add (numbers)]\nمثال: ６０にするためには１７に何を足せばよいの。\n→ What do you have to add to 17 to get 60? / جَمَعَ (To sum up; to put together mentally; to add up.) / أَضَافَ (To append (e.g. a statement); to say further information.) / أَضَافَ (To intensify; to augment; to increase.) / أَضَافَ (To add someone as a friend.)  [to add (something)]\nمثال: もしコーヒーが濃すぎれば、いくらかお湯を足して下さい。\n→ If the coffee is too strong, add some more water. / [to take care of (e.g. one's business)]",
 "足でまとい": "عَائِق, عَقَبَة (A hindrance; that which impedes or obstructs progress; impedance.)  [impediment]\nمثال: 足手まといになる子供をお頼みしてすみません。\n→ I am sorry to encumber you with the children.",
 "足どり": "مَشَى, تَمَشَّى (To move on the feet by alternately setting each foot (or pair or group of feet, ) / تمشّى (To take for a walk or accompany on a walk.) / مَسِير, سِيرَة (A trip made by walking.) / مِشْيَة (A manner of walking; a person's style of walking.)  [walk]\nمثال: 彼女の足取りは妖精のように軽やかだった。\n→ Her footsteps were as light as a fairy's. / أَثَر (A mark left as a sign of passage of a person or animal.) / لِوْحَة دَارَاتُ مَطَبُوعَة (A current-carrying conductive pathway on a printed circuit board.)  [trace (e.g. of route taken by hunted criminal)]\nمثال: 警察は容疑者の足取りがまだつかめていない。\n→ The police have found no trace of the suspect yet.",
