 "足りとも": "مُسَطَّح, مُنبَسِط (Flat and level.) / أَمْلَس, سَوِيّ (Without great variation.) / زَوْجِيّ (Of an integer, divisible by two.) / حَتَّى (In reality (used to imply an extreme example in the case mentioned).)  [(not) even]\nمثال: １円たりとも無駄使いはできない。\n→ I can't afford to waste a single yen.",
 "足りない": "نَقْص, عَدَم وُجُود (A deficiency or need (of something desirable or necessary); an absence, want, de)  [lacking]\nمثال: 寝が足りないので、今日は早めに寝ます。\n→ Because of my lack of sleep I'm going to bed early tonight. / بَطِيء (Taking a long time to move or go a short distance, or to perform an action; not ) / أَبْطَأَ, بَطَّأَ (To make (something) run, move, etc. less quickly; to reduce the speed of.)  [slow]",
 "足りる": "[to be sufficient ; to be enough]\nمثال: これだけの量の食料で一週間のキャンプに足りるでしょうか。\n→ Will this much food do for a week's camping? / اِسْتَحَقَّ (To earn, win.)  [to deserve]\nin the form に足りる after a verb / فَعَلَ, عَمِلَ (To perform; to execute.) / دُو, دُو (A syllable used in solfège to represent the first and eighth tonic of a major sc)  [to do (the job)]",
