 "践む": "[to step on ; to tread on]\nمثال: その男は私の足を踏んだのにわびることさえしなかった。\n→ The man did not so much as apologize for stepping on my foot. / زَارَ (To go and meet (a person) as an act of friendliness or sociability.) / زِيَارَة (A single act of visiting.)  [to visit] / خِبْرَة, تَجْرِبَة (The effect upon the judgment or feelings produced by any event, whether witnesse) / اِخْتِبَار (An activity one has performed.) / خِبْرَة (A collection of events and/or activities from which an individual or group may g) / خِبْرَة, تَجْرِبَة (The knowledge thus gathered.)  [to experience]\nمثال: 彼女が初舞台を踏んだのは1969年であった。\n→ Her first appearance on the stage was in 1969. / تَبِعَ, اِتَّبَعَ (To go or come after in a sequence.) / اِتَّبَعَ (To carry out (orders, instructions, etc.).) / اِتَّبَعَ (To live one's life according to (religion, teachings, etc).) / تَابَعَ, تَتَبَّعَ (To watch, to keep track of (reports of) some event or person.) / تَابَعَ (To subscribe to see content from an account on a social media platform.)  [to follow (rules, principles, etc.)]\nمثال: 何をするにも順序を踏んでやりなさい。\n→ No matter what you do, you must follow the correct order.",
