 "身がる": "رَشِيق, خَفِيف اَلْحَرَكَة (Having the faculty of quick motion in the limbs; apt or ready to move; loose-joi)  [agile]\nمثال: 捕らえることのできないもの、身軽で素早いもののたとえ、だそうです。\n→ It's apparently a metaphor for something uncatchable, light of body and fleet of foot. / إِشَارَة مُرُور, إِشَارَة ضَوْئِيَّة (A source of illumination.) / نُور, ضَوْء (A flame or something used to create fire.) / أَشْعَلَ, أَوْقَدَ (To start (a fire).) / أَضَاءَ (To illuminate; to provide light for when it is dark.) / مُنِير (Having light; bright; clear; not dark or obscure.) / فَاتِح (Pale or whitish in color; highly luminous and more or less deficient in chroma.) / خَفِيف (of low weight) / خفيف (of low weight) / خفيف (of low weight)  [light (e.g. luggage)] / مُرْتَاحُ اَلْبَالِ, خَالِي اَلْقَلْبِ (Without cares or worries; free of concern or worries; without difficulty.)  [carefree]",
