 "迂遠": "دَوَّار (A road junction at which traffic streams circularly around a central island.)  [roundabout] / جَاهِل (Unknowledgeable or uneducated; characterized by ignorance.)  [ignorant (of the world)]",
 "迂闊": "غَيْر مُبَالِي (Not giving sufficient attention or thought, especially concerning the avoidance )  [careless]\nمثال: そんな事をするとはうかつだった。\n→ It was careless of me to do something like that.",
 "迄に": "بِجَانِب, جنب (Near or next to.) / عِنْدَ, فِي (Not later than (the given time); not later than the end of (the given time inter) / مِن قِبَل, بِوَاسِطَّة (Indicates the person or thing that does or causes something: Through the action ) / بِوَاسِطَّة, لِـ (Indicates the creator of a work: Existing through the authorship etc. of.)  [by]\nمثال: 昭和天皇が靖国神社で７５年までに戦後計８回参拝した。\n→ In the post-War period, up until 1975, Emperor Showa prayed at the Yasukuni Shrine a total of 8 times.",
 "迅速": "سَرِيع (Moving with speed, rapidity or swiftness, or capable of doing so; rapid; fast.) / سَرِيعٌ (Occurring in a short time; happening or done rapidly.) / حَيٌّ (Alive, living.) / جَارٍ (Pregnant, especially at the stage where the foetus's movements can be felt; figu) / سَرِيعًا, بِسُرْعَةٍ (Quickly, in a quick manner.)  [(very) quick]\nمثال: 間髪を入れず、迅速かつ的確な応対、畏れ入ります。\n→ Such an accurate, lightning-quick reply. What can I say?",
 "迎い": "اِجْتِمَاع, مَجْلِس (A gathering of persons for a purpose; an assembly.) / مُلَاقَاة, مُقَابَلَة (An encounter between people, even accidental.) / مُلَاقَاة, لِقَاء (An administrative unit in the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers).)  [meeting]",
 "迎え": "اِجْتِمَاع, مَجْلِس (A gathering of persons for a purpose; an assembly.) / مُلَاقَاة, مُقَابَلَة (An encounter between people, even accidental.) / مُلَاقَاة, لِقَاء (An administrative unit in the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers).)  [meeting]\nمثال: そこにいて下さい。迎えに行きますから。\n→ Stay put. I'll come and get you. / [person sent to meet a visitor]",
 "迎える": "اِسْتَقْبَلَ, اِسْتَلَمَ (To take, as something that is offered; to accept.) / اِسْتَقْبَلَ, يَسْتَقْبِل (To act as a host for guests; to give admittance to; to permit to enter, as into )  [to receive]\nمثال: 医者を迎えにやったとき彼が病気になって１週間たっていた。\n→ He had been ill for a week when they sent for a doctor. / دَعَا إِلَى (To request, demand.)  [to call for]\nمثال: 彼をすぐに迎えてやることに決まった。\n→ It was decided that he should be sent for at once. / قَبِلَ (To receive, especially with a consent, with favour, or with approval.) / اِعْتَرَفَ (To admit to a place or a group.) / قَبِلَ (To receive or admit to; to agree to; to assent to; to submit to.)  [to accept (e.g. as a member of a group or family)]\nمثال: 首相は三顧の礼をもって彼を法務大臣に迎えた。\n→ The Prime Minister has won his services as Minister for Justice. / بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [to reach (a certain time, a point in one's life, etc.)]\nمثال: よいお年をお迎えください。\n→ I wish you a Happy New Year.",
 "迎え主": "مُحَافِظ (Someone who takes care of a place or thing; someone looking after a place, or re)  [caretaker (of a rescue pet)]",
 "迎え撃つ": "وَاجَهَ (To stand or meet facing, especially in competition, hostility or defiance; to co)  [to confront]",
 "迎合": "تَمْوِين (The business of providing food and related services; foodservice.)  [catering (to)]\nمثال: あの党はいつも中流階級に迎合しています。\n→ That party is always pandering to the middle class.",
 "迎撃": "اِعْتَرَضَ (To stop, deflect or divert (something in progress or motion).)  [intercept]\nمثال: このまま障壁を張っていても死ぬのを待つだけだ！だから俺たちは障壁の外に出て、敵を迎撃する、いいな！？\n→ To keep holding the barrier up is just to wait for death! So we're going to go out past the wall and counter attack the enemy, you ready!?",
 "近々": "قَرِيبًا, سَرْعَانَ مَا (Within a short time; quickly.)  [soon]\nمثال: 彼の秘密は近々あばかれるだろう。\n→ His secret will be disclosed soon. / أَغْلَقَ, سَكَّر (To remove or block an opening, gap or passage through.) / قَرِيب (Having little difference or distance in place, position, or abstractly; see also)  [close (by)]",
 "近い": "قَرِيب (Physically close.) / قَرِيبًا (At or towards a position close in space or time.) / بِٱلْقُرْب مِنَ, عِنْدَ (Physically close to, in close proximity to.) / قَرُبَ (To come closer to; to approach.)  [near]\nمثال: クリスマスが近くなってきた。\n→ Christmas is fast approaching. / أَغْلَقَ, سَكَّر (To remove or block an opening, gap or passage through.) / قَرِيب (Having little difference or distance in place, position, or abstractly; see also)  [close (in time)] / أَغْلَقَ, سَكَّر (To remove or block an opening, gap or passage through.) / قَرِيب (Having little difference or distance in place, position, or abstractly; see also)  [close (relationship)] / [closely related]",
 "近いうちに": "قَرِيبًا, سَرْعَانَ مَا (Within a short time; quickly.)  [soon]\nمثال: また近いうちにお会いましょう。\n→ I hope I'll see you again soon.",
 "近い内に": "قَرِيبًا, سَرْعَانَ مَا (Within a short time; quickly.)  [soon]\nمثال: また近いうちにお会いましょう。\n→ I hope I'll see you again soon.",
 "近く": "قَرِيب (Physically close.) / قَرِيبًا (At or towards a position close in space or time.) / بِٱلْقُرْب مِنَ, عِنْدَ (Physically close to, in close proximity to.) / قَرُبَ (To come closer to; to approach.)  [near]\nمثال: 彼女は風呂付きの部屋を探していたのだが、この近くで見つけた。\n→ She was looking for a room with a bath, and found one near here. / تَقْرِيبًا (In close approximation; almost, virtually.)  [nearly (e.g. \"it took nearly one year\")]\nمثال: ７時近くだ。学校へ行かなくては。\n→ It is close to seven o'clock. We have to go to school. / قَرِيبًا, سَرْعَانَ مَا (Within a short time; quickly.)  [soon]\nمثال: 国会は近く解散するだろう。\n→ The Diet will soon be dissolved.",
