 "近眼": "قَصَّرَ النَّظَرِ (The property of being nearsighted, myopia.)  [nearsightedness]\nمثال: 十人に一人は近眼である。\n→ One out of ten persons is nearsighted.",
 "近視": "قَصَّرَ النَّظَرِ (The property of being nearsighted, myopia.)  [nearsightedness]\nمثال: 私は近視なので、あの看板に何が書いてあるか分からない。\n→ I am near-sighted, so I cannot make out what is written on that signboard.",
 "近親姦": "زِنَا مَحَارِم, سِفَاح الْقُرْبَى (Sexual relations between close relatives, especially immediate family members an)  [incest]",
 "近親相姦": "زِنَا مَحَارِم, سِفَاح الْقُرْبَى (Sexual relations between close relatives, especially immediate family members an)  [incest]\nمثال: 議論のため、母親と息子の近親相姦が黙認されている部族社会を仮定してみよう。\n→ Imagine, for the sake of argument, a tribal group in which mother-son incest was countenanced.",
 "近辺": "جِوَار, قُرْب (The residential area near one's home.) / حَيّ (A formal or informal division of a municipality or region.) / جِوَار (The quality of being a neighbor, of living nearby, next to each other; proximity)  [neighborhood]\nمثال: この近辺で、美味しい郷土料理を食べさせてくれるお店はありますか。\n→ Is there a restaurant around here that serves local delicacies?",
 "近近": "قَرِيبًا, سَرْعَانَ مَا (Within a short time; quickly.)  [soon]\nمثال: 彼の秘密は近々あばかれるだろう。\n→ His secret will be disclosed soon. / أَغْلَقَ, سَكَّر (To remove or block an opening, gap or passage through.) / قَرِيب (Having little difference or distance in place, position, or abstractly; see also)  [close (by)]",
 "近郊": "ضَاحِيَة, مَشَارِف (A more remote part of a town or city; the periphery, environs; a suburb.)  [outskirts]\nمثال: 彼は東京近郊に住んでいる。\n→ He lives in the suburbs of Tokyo.",
 "近郷": "رِيف (An area located outside of towns and cities; an area that is not urban or suburb)  [countryside]",
 "近間": "قرب (Closeness; the state of being near in space, time, or relationship.)  [proximity]",
 "近隣": "جِوَار, قُرْب (The residential area near one's home.) / حَيّ (A formal or informal division of a municipality or region.) / جِوَار (The quality of being a neighbor, of living nearby, next to each other; proximity)  [neighborhood]\nمثال: 近隣の家は壊れたが、自宅は少しの修繕費ですんだ。\n→ The neighbouring house was destroyed, but mine survived just a bit of cost for repair.",
