 "近頃": "مُؤَخَّرًا (in the recent past) / حَدِيثًا (in the recent past) / بِأَخَرَة (in the recent past)  [recently]\nمثال: 近頃は旅行は楽だ。\n→ Travelling is easy these days. / [terribly ; awfully]",
 "返": "أَجَابَ, رَدَّ (To give a written or spoken response, especially to a question, request, accusat) / إِجَابَة, جَوَاب (A written or spoken response; part of a conversation.)  [reply]\nin telegrams",
 "返し": "رَجَعَ, عَادَ (To come or go back (to a place or person).) / أَرْجَعَ, أَعَادَ (To give something back to its original holder or owner.) / عَوْدَة (The act of returning.)  [return] / [return gift ; return favour] / [barb (on a fishing hook)] / [mixture of soy sauce, sugar and mirin]",
 "返す": "رَجَعَ, عَادَ (To come or go back (to a place or person).) / أَرْجَعَ, أَعَادَ (To give something back to its original holder or owner.) / عَوْدَة (The act of returning.)  [to return (something)]\nمثال: お金は明日返すよ。\n→ I'll give you back the money tomorrow. / قَلَبَ (To flip over; to rotate uppermost to bottom.)  [to turn over] / جَازَى (To pay (a debt or the lender) so as to provide the entire amount of money owed.)  [to pay back]\nمثال: お前は恩を仇で返したな。\n→ You bit the hand that fed you. / أَجَابَ (To say something in return; to answer; to reply.)  [to respond (with)]",
 "返り": "[turning over ; flipping over] / أَجَابَ, رَدَّ (To give a written or spoken response, especially to a question, request, accusat) / إِجَابَة, جَوَاب (A written or spoken response; part of a conversation.)  [reply] / [marks written alongside characters in a classical Chinese text to indicate their ordering when read…] / طَيَّة (Each of the two triangular pieces of cloth on the front of a jacket or coat that)  [lapel]",
 "返り事": "[message that a messenger brings back home] / أَجَابَ, رَدَّ (To give a written or spoken response, especially to a question, request, accusat) / إِجَابَة, جَوَاب (A written or spoken response; part of a conversation.)  [reply] / [return gift]",
 "返り咲き": "رِيمُونْتَادَا (An occurrence of an athlete or sports team in a competition overcoming a substan)  [comeback (e.g. in business)] / [second blooming (in a season) ; reflowering]",
 "返り咲く": "عَادَ, رَجَعَ (To return to a place.)  [to come back]\nمثال: 彼は舞台に返り咲いた。\n→ He has made a fine comeback on the stage.",
 "返り言": "[message that a messenger brings back home] / أَجَابَ, رَدَّ (To give a written or spoken response, especially to a question, request, accusat) / إِجَابَة, جَوَاب (A written or spoken response; part of a conversation.)  [reply] / [return gift]",
 "返る": "رَجَعَ, عَادَ (To come or go back (to a place or person).) / أَرْجَعَ, أَعَادَ (To give something back to its original holder or owner.) / عَوْدَة (The act of returning.)  [to return]\nesp. 返る\nمثال: のろいはのろい主に返る。\n→ Curses, like chickens, come home to roost. / قَلَبَ (To flip over; to rotate uppermost to bottom.)  [to turn over] / [to become extremely ; to become completely]\nafter the -masu stem of a verb; esp. 返る",
 "返上": "رَجَعَ, عَادَ (To come or go back (to a place or person).) / أَرْجَعَ, أَعَادَ (To give something back to its original holder or owner.) / عَوْدَة (The act of returning.)  [return]\nمثال: 私は家族のために休日を返上することに同意した。\n→ I agreed to give up my vacation for my family.",
