 "追いつめる": "زَاوِيَة, رُكْن (The point where two converging lines meet; an angle, either external or internal)  [to corner]\nمثال: 彼は追いつめられたシカを銃でねらった。\n→ He drew a bead on a stag at bay.",
 "追いはぎ": "قاطِعُ طَرِيق, قُطّاعُ ٱلطُّرُق (A person, usually mounted on horseback, who robbed travelers on public roads.)  [highwayman]\nمثال: 追い剥ぎが通行人から金を奪った。\n→ A highwayman robbed a foot passenger of his money. / [highway robbery (of money, clothing, belongings) ; holdup]",
 "追いやる": "طَرَدَ (To force someone or something to leave)  [to drive away]\nمثال: 朝日が霧をおいやった。\n→ The rising sun dispersed the mist. / [to force into an unpleasant situation (bankruptcy, prostitution, suicide, etc.)]\nمثال: これ以上の値引きは、私どもを赤字に追いやるでしょう。\n→ A further reduction would make us go into the red.",
 "追い付く": "بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [to reach]\nمثال: トムに追いつくために走らなければならなかった。\n→ I had to run to catch up with Tom. / [to be compensated ; to make up for one's losses]",
 "追い出し": "إِبْعَاد (The act of expelling or the state of being expelled.)  [expulsion] / [drum beat at the end of a day's performance (in the theatre, sumo, etc.)]",
 "追い出す": "طَرَدَ, نَفَى (To remove from membership.)  [to expel]\nمثال: 台所からその猫を追い出してくれ。\n→ Chase the cat out of the kitchen.",
 "追い切り": "مُحَاكَمَة (A meeting or series of meetings in a court of law at which evidence is presented)  [trial]",
 "追い剥ぎ": "قاطِعُ طَرِيق, قُطّاعُ ٱلطُّرُق (A person, usually mounted on horseback, who robbed travelers on public roads.)  [highwayman]\nمثال: 追い剥ぎが通行人から金を奪った。\n→ A highwayman robbed a foot passenger of his money. / [highway robbery (of money, clothing, belongings) ; holdup]",
 "追い払う": "طَرَدَ (To force someone or something to leave)  [to drive away]\nمثال: 警察は群衆を追い払った。\n→ The police turned away the crowd.",
 "追い抜き": "سَبَقَ (To pass a slower moving object or entity (on the side closest to oncoming traffi)  [overtaking] / [pursuit (event)]",
 "追い抜く": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [to pass (a car)] / فَاقَ, تَجَاوَزَ (To go beyond or exceed (something) in an adjudicative or literal sense.)  [to surpass]",
 "追い掛ける": "طَارَدَ (To pursue.)  [to chase]\nمثال: 犬が猫を追いかけていた。\n→ A dog was running after a cat. / آنَذَاكَ, حِينَئِذٍ (At that time.) / ثُمَّ (Soon afterward.) / ثُمَّ (Next in order of place.) / إِذًا, إِذَنْ (In that case.)  [(and) then]\nas 追いかけて or 追いかけるように",
 "追い散らす": "طَرَدَ (To force someone or something to leave)  [to drive away]",
 "追い求める": "لَاحَقَ (To follow urgently, originally with intent to capture or harm; to chase.) / اِتَّبَعَ (To follow, travel down (a particular way, course of action etc.).)  [to pursue]\nمثال: 若者は自分が追い求めているものがわかっていないようだ。\n→ Young men and women don't seem to know what they are seeking after.",
 "追い立て": "طَرْد (The act of evicting.)  [eviction]",
 "追い立てる": "[to drive on ; to urge forward (e.g. cattle)] / أَجْلَى, طَرَدَ (To expel (one or more people) from their property; to force (one or more people))  [to evict]",
 "追い落し": "طَرَدَ (To expel; to remove.)  [ousting] / [connect-and-die ; oiotoshi]",
 "追い落とし": "طَرَدَ (To expel; to remove.)  [ousting] / [connect-and-die ; oiotoshi]",
 "追い落とす": "طَرَدَ (To expel; to remove.)  [to oust]\nمثال: 彼は若い人のグループにその職から追い落とされた。\n→ He was edged out of office by a group of younger men. / [to drive down (e.g. into a valley) ; to chase down] / أَسْر (An act of capturing; a seizing by force or stratagem.) / أَسَرَ (To take control of; to seize by force or stratagem.)  [to capture (a castle)] / طَرَدَ (To force someone or something to leave)  [to drive away (e.g. from the capital)]",
 "追い詰める": "زَاوِيَة, رُكْن (The point where two converging lines meet; an angle, either external or internal)  [to corner]\nمثال: 彼は追いつめられたシカを銃でねらった。\n→ He drew a bead on a stag at bay.",
 "追い越し": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing]",
 "追い越す": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [to pass (e.g. car)]\nمثال: うさぎはかめに追い越された。\n→ The hare was outdistanced by the tortoise. / فَاقَ, تَجَاوَزَ (To go beyond or exceed (something) in an adjudicative or literal sense.)  [to surpass]",
 "追い込み": "[final stage ; final stretch] / [live printing area (in publishing)] / مَعْرِض, صَالَةُ عَرْض (An institution, building, or room for the exhibition and conservation of importa)  [gallery (in a theatre)] / سِيَاقَة, قِيَادَة (In particular, the action of operating a motor vehicle.)  [driving (animals, fish, etc.)]",
 "追い込む": "قَطِيع (A number of domestic animals assembled together under the watch or ownership of ) / قَطِيع (Any collection of animals gathered or travelling in a company.) / قَطِيع (A crowd, a mass of people or things; a rabble.) / رَعَى (intr: to unite or associate in a herd) / رَاعٍ (Someone who keeps a group of domestic animals.) / رَعَى (To act as a herdsman or a shepherd.) / رَعَى (To form or put into a herd.)  [to herd] / زَاوِيَة, رُكْن (The point where two converging lines meet; an angle, either external or internal)  [to corner]\nمثال: とうとう土壇場に追い込まれた。\n→ We have been completely cornered. / [to go hard ; to push yourself]\nمثال: 僕は追い込まれると一番仕事をする。\n→ I work best under pressure. / [to run on (e.g. lines in printing)]",
 "追い返す": "طَرَدَ (To force someone or something to leave)  [to drive away]\nمثال: 強面の変なセールスだったらすぐアタシを呼びなさいね、追い返してやるから。\n→ If it's an aggressive strange salesman, then call me right away. I'll chase him off.",
 "追い追い": "شَيْئاً فَشَيْئاً, خُطْوةً فَخُطْوةً (In a gradual manner; making slow progress; slowly.)  [gradually]",
 "追う": "طَارَدَ (To pursue.)  [to chase]\nمثال: その警官は泥棒を追っていた。\n→ The policeman was after the thief. / تَبِعَ, اِتَّبَعَ (To go or come after in a sequence.) / اِتَّبَعَ (To carry out (orders, instructions, etc.).) / اِتَّبَعَ (To live one's life according to (religion, teachings, etc).) / تَابَعَ, تَتَبَّعَ (To watch, to keep track of (reports of) some event or person.) / تَابَعَ (To subscribe to see content from an account on a social media platform.)  [to follow (a set order, a trend, etc.)]\nمثال: エイズ調査の分野におけるすべての変化を追い続けることはできない。\n→ I can't keep track of all the changes taking place in the world of AIDS research. / طَرَدَ (To push or to pull, i.e. to force, (someone or something) out of somewhere.)  [to drive out] / قَادَ, سَاقَ (To operate a vehicle:) / سَاقَ (To compel to move:) / سَاقَ (To cause to move by the application of physical force:)  [to drive (e.g. a herd)]\nمثال: カウボーイが牛を牧草地へ追っていく。\n→ A cowboy is driving cattle to the pasture.",
 "追ける": "تَبِعَ, اِتَّبَعَ (To go or come after in a sequence.) / اِتَّبَعَ (To carry out (orders, instructions, etc.).) / اِتَّبَعَ (To live one's life according to (religion, teachings, etc).) / تَابَعَ, تَتَبَّعَ (To watch, to keep track of (reports of) some event or person.) / تَابَعَ (To subscribe to see content from an account on a social media platform.)  [to follow (someone)]\nمثال: その男がつけてくることに気づいて彼女は恐くなった。\n→ She became scared when she noticed the man following her.",
 "追っかけ": "طَارَدَ (To pursue.)  [chase] / [chase scene (in a movie)] / [obsessive fan who follows a celebrity around ; groupie]\nمثال: アイドルのコンサート会場に、追っかけのファンがウジャウジャ集まっていた。\n→ At the pop star's concert the fans were swarming around the foot of the stage. / قَرِيبًا, سَرْعَانَ مَا (Within a short time; quickly.)  [soon (after)]",
