 "途方もない": "اِسْتِثْنَائِيّ, غَيْرُ عَادِيّ (Out of the ordinary; exceptional; unusual.)  [extraordinary]\nمثال: そんな途方もない話は聞いたことがない。\n→ That's the damnedest story I ever heard.",
 "途方も無い": "اِسْتِثْنَائِيّ, غَيْرُ عَادِيّ (Out of the ordinary; exceptional; unusual.)  [extraordinary]\nمثال: そんな途方もない話は聞いたことがない。\n→ That's the damnedest story I ever heard.",
 "途端": "عَدْل (Morally right; upright, righteous, equitable; fair.) / فَقَط (only, simply, merely)  [just (now, at the moment, etc.)]\nمثال: これをきいたとたん、彼は真っ青になった。\n→ On hearing this, he turned pale.",
 "途端に": "مَا أَن, حَالَمَا (At the moment when; immediately (after); instantly; directly.)  [as soon as]\nمثال: その知らせを聞いた途端に、彼は青ざめた。\n→ On hearing the news, he turned pale.",
 "途絶": "مُقَاطَعَة (The act of interrupting, or the state of being interrupted.)  [interruption]",
 "途絶え": "تَوَقَّفَ (To interrupt an activity and wait.) / تَوَقُّف, وَقْف (A temporary stop or rest; an intermission of action; interruption; suspension; c)  [pause]",
 "途絶える": "وَقَفَ, تَوَقَّفَ (To cease moving.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to cease moving or progressing.) / تَوَقَّفَ, وَقَّف (To cease; to no longer continue.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to come to an end.) / مَوْقِف (A (usually marked) place where buses, trams or trains halt to let passengers get) / وَقْفَة (An action of stopping; interruption of travel.)  [to stop]\nمثال: その飛行機からの通信が突然とだえた。\n→ All communication with that airplane was suddenly cut off.",
 "途轍もない": "مُسْرِف (Profuse in expenditure; prodigal; wasteful.)  [extravagant]\nمثال: その地震はとてつもなく大きな津波を引き起こした。\n→ The earthquake created a tremendous sea wave. / ضَخْم, هَائِل (Extremely large; greatly exceeding the common size, extent, etc.)  [enormous]",
 "逗留": "مَكَثَ, بَقِيَ (To remain in a particular place, especially for a definite or short period of ti) / إِقَامَة (Continuance or a period of time spent in a place; abode for an indefinite time.)  [stay]",
 "逗留客": "زَائِر (Someone who visits someone else; someone staying as a guest.) / زَائِر, سَائِح (An extraterrestrial being on Earth.)  [visitor]",
 "這々の体": "تَهَافَتَ (To struggle eagerly with others for something thrown upon the ground; to go down)  [scrambling]",
 "這いずる": "زَحَفَ, دَبَّ (To move over (an area) on hands and knees, or by dragging the body along.)  [to crawl]",
 "這い上がる": "[to creep up ; to crawl up]\nمثال: 何かが私の腕をはい上がってくるのを感じた。\n→ I felt something crawling up my arm. / هَزَمَ, غَلَبَ (To surmount (a physical or abstract obstacle); to prevail over, to get the bette)  [to overcome (a bad situation)]",
 "這い上る": "[to creep up ; to crawl up]\nمثال: 何かが私の腕をはい上がってくるのを感じた。\n→ I felt something crawling up my arm. / هَزَمَ, غَلَبَ (To surmount (a physical or abstract obstacle); to prevail over, to get the bette)  [to overcome (a bad situation)]",
 "這う": "زَحَفَ, دَبَّ (To move over (an area) on hands and knees, or by dragging the body along.)  [to crawl]\nمثال: 赤ん坊は歩く前にはう。\n→ Babies crawl before they walk. / [to slither ; to wriggle] / جَرَّ (drag behind) / أَثَر (The track or indication marking the route followed by something that has passed,) / مَسْلَك (A route for travel over land, especially a narrow, unpaved pathway for use by hi)  [to trail (of vines, flowers, etc.)]",
 "這う這うの体": "تَهَافَتَ (To struggle eagerly with others for something thrown upon the ground; to go down)  [scrambling]",
 "這般": "هٰذِهِ, هٰؤُلَاءِ (plural of this)  [these]",
 "這裏": "دَاخِل (In the inner part, spatially; physically inside.) / في غضون (In the scope or range of.) / فِي خِلَال (Before the specified duration ends.)  [within]",
 "這這の体": "تَهَافَتَ (To struggle eagerly with others for something thrown upon the ground; to go down)  [scrambling]",
 "通": "سُلْطَة (Power or right to make or enforce rules, give orders, or impose obligation; or a)  [authority]\nمثال: コーヒー通の人達に結構評判がいいそうです。\n→ I hear that it has quite the reputation with coffee connoisseurs. / [counter for messages, letters, notes, documents, etc.]\nمثال: ここにあなたあての手紙が何通かあります。\n→ Here are some letters for you. / فَهْم (The act of one that understands or comprehends; the mental process of discernmen) / رُؤْيَة (Opinion, judgement, or outlook.) / تَفَاهُم (An agreement of minds; harmony; something mutually understood or agreed upon.) / فهم (Showing compassion, tolerance, and forbearance; sympathetically aware.)  [understanding (esp. of male-female relations)] / [supernatural powers ; magical powers]",
 "通い": "[coming and going ; going back and forth (between)] / مُتَكَرِّر (Done or occurring often; common.) / اِرْتَادَ (To visit often.)  [frequenting] / دَفْتَر اِدِّخَار (wealth)  [bankbook]",
 "通い帳": "دَفْتَر اِدِّخَار (wealth)  [bankbook]",
 "通い船": "مُعَدِّيَة, عَبَّارَة (A boat or ship used to transport people, smaller vehicles and goods from one por)  [ferry]",
 "通い路": "طَرِيق, مَسار (A course or way which is traveled or passed.)  [route]",
 "通う": "[to go to and from (a place) ; to go back and forth between] / حَضَرَ ((''ambitransitive'') to be present at or regularly go to)  [to attend]\nمثال: ６歳以上の子供は学校に通わなければならない。\n→ Children of six and above should attend school. / [to circulate (e.g. blood, electricity) ; to be communicated (e.g. thought)] / شَبِهَ (to be like or similar to something else) / مَاثَلَ (to be like or similar to something else)  [to resemble]",
 "通し": "[continuing from beginning to end ; continuous run] / مَزَّة, مُشَهْي (A small, light, and usually savory first course in a meal.)  [appetizer]\nusu. お通し / [performance of an entire play]",
 "通じ": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [(bowel) movement]\nusu. お〜\nمثال: お通じがよくなりますよ。\n→ It moves the bowels. / فَهْم (The act of one that understands or comprehends; the mental process of discernmen) / رُؤْيَة (Opinion, judgement, or outlook.) / تَفَاهُم (An agreement of minds; harmony; something mutually understood or agreed upon.) / فهم (Showing compassion, tolerance, and forbearance; sympathetically aware.)  [understanding (of another's thoughts, feelings, etc.)]",
 "通じて": "عَبْر (From one side or end of (something) to the other.) / خِلَالَ, عَبْرَ (From one side or end of (something) to the other.) / فِي (Amidst or surrounded by (while moving).) / بِوَاسِطَة (By means of.)  [through]\nas を～\nمثال: カタログを通じて郵便で買い物をすることによって、人々は幅広い商品を選ぶことが出来る。\n→ Shopping by mail through catalogs gives people a wide choice of merchandise. / طَوَال (In every part of; all through.) / طَوَال (In every part; everywhere.)  [throughout (e.g. the year)]\nas を～\nمثال: この国では年間を通じて気温の変動がほとんどない。\n→ This country has an even temperature throughout the year. / عُمُومًا (Popularly or widely.) / بِوَجْهٍ عَامّ (Without reference to specific details.)  [generally]",
 "通じる": "رَصَاص (A heavy, pliable, inelastic metal element, having a bright, bluish color, but ea) / قَادَ (To guide or conduct.) / أَرْشَدَ, هَدَى (To guide or conduct.)  [to lead (to)]\nمثال: その道は駅に通じている。\n→ This road leads to the station. / تَدَفُّق (the movement of a fluid) / تَدَفَّقَ, سَالَ (To move as a fluid from one position to another.)  [to flow (of a liquid, current, etc.)]\nمثال: この辺にはガスが通じてますか。\n→ Is gas available in this neighborhood? / [to be conveyed (of an intention, meaning, etc.) ; to be understood (by)]\nمثال: 彼にはロシア語が通じる。\n→ He is learned in Russian. / [to be well versed (in) ; to be proficient (in)]\noft. as 通じている\nمثال: 彼は外国事情に通じている。\n→ He is well versed in foreign affairs.",
 "通じ薬": "مُلَيّن (Having the effect of moving the bowels, or aiding digestion and preventing const)  [laxative]",
 "通す": "[to let pass ; to allow through]\nمثال: 彼はトラックを通すために車を横に寄せた。\n→ He pulled aside to let a truck pass. / [to transmit (e.g. light, sound, etc.) ; to conduct (electricity)]\nمثال: 銅はよく電気を通す。\n→ Copper conducts electricity well. / خَيْط, خيط (A cord formed by spinning or twisting together textile fibers or filaments into ) / خَيْط (A unit of execution, lighter in weight than a process, usually sharing memory an) / مَوْضُوع (A series of posts or messages, consisting of an initial post and responses to it)  [to thread (e.g. a needle)]\nمثال: 針に糸を通すことができないので縫い物は好きではありません。\n→ I don't like sewing because I can't thread the needle. / رَبَطَ (to join two or more pieces)  [to connect (e.g. two places)]\nمثال: 山を通してトンネルを通した。\n→ They drove a tunnel through the hill.",
 "通ずる": "رَصَاص (A heavy, pliable, inelastic metal element, having a bright, bluish color, but ea) / قَادَ (To guide or conduct.) / أَرْشَدَ, هَدَى (To guide or conduct.)  [to lead (to)]\nمثال: すべての道はローマに通ず。\n→ All roads lead to Rome. / تَدَفُّق (the movement of a fluid) / تَدَفَّقَ, سَالَ (To move as a fluid from one position to another.)  [to flow (of a liquid, current, etc.)] / [to be conveyed (of an intention, meaning, etc.) ; to be understood (by)] / [to be well versed (in) ; to be proficient (in)]\noft. as 通じている",
 "通り": "شَارِع, زَنَقَة (A paved part of road, usually in a village or a town.)  [street]\nمثال: この通りに沿って行けば駅に着きます。\n→ If you follow this street, you will get to the station. / مُرُور (pedestrians or vehicles on roads or on the air)  [traffic]\nمثال: この横町は人の通りが多い。\n→ This cross street is busy with pedestrian traffic. / تَدَفُّق (the movement of a fluid) / تَدَفَّقَ, سَالَ (To move as a fluid from one position to another.)  [flow (of water, air, etc.)]\nمثال: この煙突は通りが悪くなった。\n→ This chimney has begun to draw badly. / بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [reach (of voice)]",
