 "通りがかり": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing (along the way)]\nمثال: 通りがかりの車が私たちに水をはねた。\n→ A passing car splashed water on us.",
 "通りすぎる": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [to pass]\nمثال: 私はその暗い道を通り過ぎた。\n→ I passed over the dark street.",
 "通りぬける": "اِخْتَرَقَ, نَفَذَ (To go through, to travel through, to transit or lie across a place or from one p)  [to pass through]\nمثال: その車は門を通り抜けた。\n→ The car passed through a gate.",
