 "通り掛かり": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing (along the way)]\nمثال: 通りがかりの車が私たちに水をはねた。\n→ A passing car splashed water on us.",
 "通り掛け": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing (along the way)]\nمثال: 通りがけに本屋によった。\n→ I entered the bookstore on the way.",
 "通り掛り": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing (along the way)]\nمثال: 通りがかりの車が私たちに水をはねた。\n→ A passing car splashed water on us.",
 "通り過ぎる": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [to pass]\nمثال: 私はその暗い道を通り過ぎた。\n→ I passed over the dark street.",
 "通り道": "قِطْعَة (A paragraph or section of text or music with particular meaning.)  [passage]\nمثال: 警官が通り道を空けて車を通した。\n→ Policemen cleared the way to let cars pass.",
 "通り雨": "شَتْوَة, مَطْرَة (A brief fall of precipitation (spell of rain, or a similar fall of snow, sleet, ) / مِرَشَّة, دُش (A device for bathing by which water is made to fall on the body from a height, e) / اِسْتَحَمَّ, تَحَمَّمَ (To bathe using a shower.)  [shower]\nمثال: 通り雨だからすぐ止むよ。\n→ This is a tropical storm. It'll be over soon.",
 "通り魔的": "عَشْوَائِيّ (Occurring for no particular reason; haphazard, unpredictable.) / عَشْوَائِيّ (Involving an outcome which is impossible to predict, but which may be represente)  [random (e.g. attack, killing)]",
 "通る": "[to go by ; to go past]\nمثال: 私は毎日その教会の前を通る。\n→ I go by that church every day. / رَكَضَ (to move quickly on two feet) / جَرَى (to move quickly on two feet)  [to run (between; of a rail service, bus route, etc.)]\nمثال: 駅と飛行機の間は、バスが通っている。\n→ Buses run between the station and the airport. / [to go indoors ; to go into a room] / اِخْتَرَقَ (To enter into; to make way into the interior of; to pierce.)  [to penetrate]\nمثال: 弾がヘルメットを通った。\n→ A bullet pierced the helmet.",
 "通事": "مُتَرْجِم, مُتَرْجِمَة (A person or thing that interprets the meaning of something for another)  [interpreter (esp. of Dutch and Chinese during the Edo period)] / [court interpreter]",
 "通例": "عَادَة, عُرْف (Frequent repetition of the same behavior; way of behavior common to many; ordina)  [custom]\nمثال: 通例、喫煙は許可していません。\n→ As a rule, we don't allow smoking. / عَادَةً, الاَكْثِرْ (Most of the time; less than always, but more than occasionally.)  [usually]",
 "通俗": "مَحْبُوب (Liked by many people; generally pleasing, widely admired.)  [popular]",
 "通俗的": "مَحْبُوب (Liked by many people; generally pleasing, widely admired.)  [popular]",
 "通信": "مُرَاسَلَة (Mutual communication or discourse:)  [correspondence]\nمثال: 彼は、無電で通信を送った。\n→ He sent a message by wireless.",
 "通信事業者": "نَاقِل (A person or company in the business of shipping freight.) / مَوْجَة حامِلة (A signal such as radio, sound, or light that is modulated to transmit informatio) / حَامِل, حَمَلَة (A person or other organism that has a genetic trait, mutation or infection liabl)  [carrier]",
 "通信員": "مُرَاسِل, مُرَاسِلَة (A journalist who sends reports back to a newspaper or radio or television statio)  [correspondent]\nمثال: 通信員は海外生活にすぐに順応しなくてはいけない。\n→ A correspondent must soon adjust himself to life abroad.",
 "通信文": "رِسَالَة, خَبَر (A communication, or what is communicated; any concept or information conveyed.)  [message]\nمثال: 今日では、アメリカで世界中のどこへ電報を打つにも電話で通信文を告げるだけでよい。\n→ Today, to send a telegram in the States to anywhere in the world, all you have to do is to give the message over the telephone.",
 "通信社": "وَكَالَةُ أَنْبَاء (An organisation that gathers and distributes news to newspapers and radio and te)  [news agency]",
 "通信簿": "التقرير المدرسي عن الطالب (A document, on cardboard or plain paper, indicating the grades that a student ha)  [report card]\nمثال: 彼の通信簿はオールＡだよ。\n→ He has a straight-A report card.",
 "通信規約": "بْرُوتُوكُول (A set of formal rules describing how to transmit or exchange data, especially ac)  [protocol]",
 "通信路": "قَنَاة (The navigable part of a river.) / قَنَاة (A specific radio frequency or band of frequencies used for transmitting televisi)  [channel]",
 "通信量": "مُرُور (pedestrians or vehicles on roads or on the air)  [traffic]",
 "通券": "تَذْكِرَة (A small document that acts as proof of something, often thereby granting the hol) / تذكرة (A service request, used to track complaints or requests that an issue be handled)  [ticket]",
 "通勤ラッシュ": "سَاعَة اَلذُّرْوَة (The times of the day when traffic jams are commonplace, due mainly to people com)  [rush hour]",
 "通名": "لَقَب (familiar, invented given name) / كُنْيَة (familiar, invented given name) / اِسْم الدَّلَع (familiar, invented given name)  [nickname]",
 "通告": "إِعْلَان, بَلَاغ (That which conveys what is announced.)  [announcement]\nمثال: 次の会合の日取りをご通告下さい。\n→ Please advise me of the date for the next meeting.",
 "通商": "تِجَارَة (The exchange or buying and selling of commodities; especially the exchange of me)  [commerce]\nمثال: わが国は米国で通商している。\n→ We do business with the United States.",
 "通報": "وَصَفَ, أَبْلَغَ (To relate details of (an event or incident); to recount, describe (something).) / أَبْلَغَ (To notify someone of (particular intelligence, suspicions, illegality, misconduc) / تَقْرِير, بَلَاغ (A piece of information describing, or an account of certain events given or pres)  [report]\nمثال: すぐ警察に通報してください。\n→ You should notify the police at once. / رِسَالَة, خَبَر (A communication, or what is communicated; any concept or information conveyed.)  [message (in information and communication theory)]",
 "通夜": "أَيْقَظَ ((often followed by up) To make somebody stop sleeping; to rouse from sleep.)  [wake]",
 "通婚": "زَوَاج, نِكَاح (The state of being married.) / زَوَاج (A union of two or more people that creates a family tie and carries legal, socia) / عُرْس, زِفَاف (A wedding; a ceremony in which people wed.)  [marriage] / [intermarriage]",
 "通学服": "زِي مَدْرَسِيّ (A number of uniform items which must be worn by pupils/students in a school.)  [school uniform]",
 "通宝": "عُمْلَة (Money or other items used to facilitate transactions.)  [currency]\nused primarily on ancient Japanese coins",
 "通帳": "دَفْتَر اِدِّخَار (wealth)  [bankbook]\nمثال: 私は自分の通帳を見たが、幸運にも５０ドル余分に入っていた。\n→ I looked at my bank account book, and happily discovered that I had an extra $50!",
 "通常": "عَادِيّ (Most commonly occurring; typical.)  [usual]\nمثال: 彼は、通常バスで学校へ行きます。\n→ He usually goes to school by bus.",
 "通常どおり": "كَالْعَادَة, كَالْمُعْتَاد (As is usually the case.)  [as usual]",
 "通常なら": "عَادَةً, الاَكْثِرْ (Most of the time; less than always, but more than occasionally.)  [usually]",
 "通常の場合": "عَادَةً, الاَكْثِرْ (Most of the time; less than always, but more than occasionally.)  [usually]",
