 "逶迱": "رِيح, ريح (One of the four elements of the ancient Greeks and Romans; air.) / لَفَّ (To turn coils (of a cord or something similar) around something.)  [winding]",
 "逸": "أَكْثَر, أَغْلَب (superlative degree of many: the majority of; more than half of (construed withou) / جِدًّا (To a great extent or degree; highly; very.)  [most]",
 "逸す": "فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [to lose (a chance)] / صَفَحَ (To pretend not to have noticed (something, especially a mistake or flaw); to pas)  [to overlook] / [to deviate ; to depart from (the norm, etc.)]",
 "逸する": "فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [to lose (a chance)]\nمثال: 君は常軌を逸しているよ。\n→ You are way off track. / صَفَحَ (To pretend not to have noticed (something, especially a mistake or flaw); to pas)  [to overlook] / [to deviate]",
 "逸らす": "[to turn away (one's eyes, face, etc.) ; to avert]\nمثال: わたしの気を仕事からそらさないでください。\n→ Please don't take my mind off the work. / أَزْعَجَ (To disturb or irritate, especially by continued or repeated acts; to bother with)  [to annoy]\nusu. in the negative / أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [to miss (the target, ball, etc.)]",
 "逸り気": "نَفَاد صَبْر (The quality of being impatient; lacking patience; restlessness and intolerance o)  [impatience]",
 "逸る": "اُغْرُب عَن وَجْهِي!, إِبْتَعِد عَنِّي! (Used to rudely tell somebody to go away or leave one alone.) / ضَلَّ الطَّرِيق (To lose one's way.)  [to get lost]",
 "逸る気持ち": "حَمَاس, حَمَاسَة (An intensity of feeling; an excited interest or eagerness.)  [enthusiasm]",
 "逸れる": "[to turn away ; to bear off] / ضَلَّ (To develop bad habits; to behave improperly or illegally.) / ضَلَّ (To come to believe an untruth.)  [to go astray]\nمثال: 本題からそれないようにしましょう。\n→ Let's not deviate from the subject.",
 "逸事": "نَادِرَة (short account of an incident) / أُطْرُوفَة (short account of an incident) / أُفْكُوهَة (short account of an incident) / طُرْفَة (short account of an incident) / فُكَاهَة (short account of an incident) / لَطِيفَة (short account of an incident)  [anecdote]",
 "逸出": "هَرَبَ (To get free; to free oneself.) / فِرَار, هُرُوب (The act of leaving a dangerous or unpleasant situation.)  [escape] / تَقَدُّم (The status of being preeminent, dominant or ascendant.)  [preeminence]",
 "逸品": "تُحْفَة, رَائِعَة (A piece of work that has been given much critical praise, especially one that is)  [masterpiece]\nمثال: これらの花は彼女の庭で咲いた逸品である。\n→ These flowers are the choice of her garden.",
 "逸失": "فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [losing (something)]",
