 "遁走": "طَيَرَان (act of flying) / تَحْلِيق (act of flying) / طَيَرَان (journey made by an aircraft) / فِرَار, هُرُوب (The act of fleeing.)  [flight]",
 "遁走曲": "فُوغَا, فُوغَا (A contrapuntal piece of music wherein a particular melody is played in a number )  [fugue]",
 "遁辞": "عَذَرَ (To forgive; to pardon; to overlook.) / اِعْتَذَرَ (To allow to leave, or release from any obligation.) / عُذْر (An explanation designed to avoid or alleviate guilt or negative judgment; a plea)  [excuse]",
 "遂": "نِهَايَة, غَايَة (The most extreme point of an object, especially one that is longer than it is wi) / غَايَة (A purpose, goal, or aim.) / اِنْتَهَى, أَنْهَى (To finish, terminate.)  [end] / مَوْت (cessation of life) / وَفَاة (cessation of life) / هَلَاك (cessation of life) / مَنِيَّة (cessation of life) / حِمَام (cessation of life) / موت (cessation of life)  [death] / أَبَدًا (At no time; on no occasion; in no circumstance.)  [never]",
 "遂げる": "أَدَّى (To finish successfully.)  [to accomplish]\nمثال: 浪士は本懐を遂げた。\n→ The rōnin attained their long-cherished ambition. / [to arrive at (a certain outcome) ; to come to]",
 "遂に": "أَخِيراً (At the end or conclusion; ultimately.)  [finally]\nمثال: ついに病気で疲れた男たちは彼が待っている山岳都市に到着した。\n→ Finally, the sick, tired men reached the mountain town where he was waiting. / فِي النِّهَايَة (Anyway, in any case; indicates a statement is true regardless of other considera)  [after all]\nwith neg. verb",
 "遂行": "تَنْفِيذ (The act of accomplishing; completion; fulfilment.)  [accomplishment]\nمثال: クーデターは慎重に遂行された。\n→ The coup was meticulously executed.",
 "遅々": "بَطِيء (Taking a long time to move or go a short distance, or to perform an action; not ) / أَبْطَأَ, بَطَّأَ (To make (something) run, move, etc. less quickly; to reduce the speed of.)  [slow]\nمثال: その国民の社会生活に関する限りでは、進歩は実に遅々たるものである。\n→ Progress has been very slow indeed, so far as the social life of the people is concerned.",
 "遅い": "بَطِيء (Taking a long time to move or go a short distance, or to perform an action; not ) / أَبْطَأَ, بَطَّأَ (To make (something) run, move, etc. less quickly; to reduce the speed of.)  [slow]\nocc. written as 鈍い\nمثال: 彼女は走るのが遅い。\n→ She is a slow runner. / مُتَأَخِّر (Near the end of a period of time.) / مُتَأَخِّر (Not arriving or occurring until after an expected time.) / مَرْحُوم (Recently deceased, dead: used particularly when speaking of the dead person's ac) / مُتَأَخِّرًا (After a deadline has passed, past a designated time.)  [late]\nocc. written as 晩い\nمثال: ジムの父はいつも帰宅が遅い。\n→ Jim's father always comes home late. / [too late]\nusu. as もう〜 or もはや〜; occ. written as 晩い",
 "遅かれ早かれ": "عَاجِلاً أَم آجِلاً, عَاجِلاً أَو آجِلاً (Eventually, at some undetermined time in the not-too-distant future.)  [sooner or later]\nمثال: 遅かれ早かれ彼は破滅する。\n→ He will eventually ruin himself.",
 "遅く": "مُتَأَخِّر (Near the end of a period of time.) / مُتَأَخِّر (Not arriving or occurring until after an expected time.) / مَرْحُوم (Recently deceased, dead: used particularly when speaking of the dead person's ac) / مُتَأَخِّرًا (After a deadline has passed, past a designated time.)  [late] / بِبُطْء (At a slow pace.)  [slowly]",
 "遅し": "بَطِيء (Taking a long time to move or go a short distance, or to perform an action; not ) / أَبْطَأَ, بَطَّأَ (To make (something) run, move, etc. less quickly; to reduce the speed of.)  [slow]",
 "遅す": "تَأْخِير, تَأَخَّر (A period of time before an event occurs; the act of delaying; procrastination; l) / أَجَّلَ, أَبْطَأَ (To put off until a later time; to defer.)  [to delay]",
 "遅らす": "تَأْخِير, تَأَخَّر (A period of time before an event occurs; the act of delaying; procrastination; l) / أَجَّلَ, أَبْطَأَ (To put off until a later time; to defer.)  [to delay]",
